        "x": "910",
        "y": "1042",
        "width": "380",
        "height": "197",
        "name": "ROUNDED_RECTANGLE"
      },
      "text": "START MODERATE\nGroup exercises at full dose and progressive strengthening within the pain rules. Full core battery."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:8350",
      "type": "connector",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "1:8350",
        "x": "1100",
        "y": "912",
        "connectorStart": "1:7243",
        "connectorStartCap": "NONE",
        "connectorEnd": "1:7255",
        "connectorEndCap": "ARROW_LINES"
      },
      "text": "NS4-1b&gt;NS4-MD"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:7259",
      "type": "shape-with-text",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "1:7259",
        "x": "1360",
        "y": "1042",
        "width": "380",
        "height": "197",
        "name": "ROUNDED_RECTANGLE"
      },
      "text": "START STRONGER\nCore programme loading, carrying and overhead work, return to sport or heavy tasks. Full core battery."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:8354",
      "type": "connector",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "1:8354",
        "x": "1550",
        "y": "912",
        "connectorStart": "1:7247",
        "connectorStartCap": "NONE",
        "connectorEnd": "1:7259",
        "connectorEndCap": "ARROW_LINES"
      },
      "text": "NS4-1c&gt;NS4-LO"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:7263",
      "type": "shape-with-text",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "1:7263",
        "x": "720",
        "y": "1374",
        "width": "760",
        "height": "332",
        "name": "ROUNDED_RECTANGLE"
      },
      "text": "NS4-2 · Short-form Örebro Musculoskeletal Pain Screening Questionnaire (10 questions)\nScores the risk of long-term disability from pain, beliefs, mood and work factors across any musculoskeletal pain site. A cut-off of 50 identified 83–85% of the people who went on to develop disability (Linton 2011).\n• Lower risk: advice, reassurance, the group’s exercises at home; few contacts.\n• Higher risk (50 or more): psychologically informed physiotherapy — tackle fears and beliefs, graded exposure, pacing, goal-setting; involve a counsellor or doctor for low mood or stress-reaction symptoms (especially after whiplash)."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:8366",
      "type": "connector",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "1:8366",
        "x": "1100",
        "y": "1245",
        "connectorStart": "1:7259",
        "connectorStartCap": "NONE",
        "connectorEnd": "1:7263",
        "connectorEndCap": "ARROW_LINES"
      },
      "text": "NS4-LO&gt;NS4-2"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:8362",
      "type": "connector",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "1:8362",
        "x": "1100",
        "y": "1245",
        "connectorStart": "1:7255",
        "connectorStartCap": "NONE",
        "connectorEnd": "1:7263",
        "connectorEndCap": "ARROW_LINES"
      },
      "text": "NS4-MD&gt;NS4-2"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:8358",
      "type": "connector",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "1:8358",
        "x": "650",
        "y": "1270",
        "connectorStart": "1:7251",
        "connectorStartCap": "NONE",
        "connectorEnd": "1:7263",
        "connectorEndCap": "ARROW_LINES"
      },
      "text": "NS4-HI&gt;NS4-2"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:7267",
      "type": "shape-with-text",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "1:7267",
        "x": "120",
        "y": "1816",
        "width": "680",
        "height": "604",
        "name": "ROUNDED_RECTANGLE"
      },
      "text": "NS4-3 · CORE BASELINE BATTERY (about 10 minutes)\nNeeds: a chair, a stopwatch, a phone and a tape measure. Repeat the SAME set at week 0, 4 and 12.\n1. Pain 0–10 (faces version for low literacy): average and worst in the last week; arm pain and headache scored separately if present.\n2. Patient-Specific Functional Scale (PSFS): the patient names their 3 hardest tasks and rates each 0–10 — this becomes the goal list. Prompt with local tasks: carrying head-loads or water, sewing or computer work, looking up to hang washing, driving or riding a two-wheeler, sleeping, floor work.\n3. Neck Disability Index (NDI): 10 items, 0–50 — check for a validated Hindi or Marathi version.\n4. Body chart: where the symptoms reach — watch arm symptoms centralise across visits.\n5. Neck range: rotation, side-bend, looking up and down (phone inclinometer app, or chin-to-shoulder distance).\n6. Deep-neck-flexor endurance hold (seconds).\n7. Thoracic rotation in sitting and chest expansion at nipple level (tape measure).\n8. Grip strength (dynamometer if available) or a timed bag-carry.\n9. Nerve check if any arm symptoms: hand-on-head sign, upper-limb tension test, strength and feeling by root."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:8370",
      "type": "connector",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "1:8370",
        "x": "460",
        "y": "1712",
        "connectorStart": "1:7263",
        "connectorStartCap": "NONE",
        "connectorEnd": "1:7267",
        "connectorEndCap": "ARROW_LINES"
      },
      "text": "NS4-2&gt;NS4-3"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:7271",
      "type": "shape-with-text",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "1:7271",
        "x": "870",
        "y": "1816",
        "width": "680",
        "height": "510",
        "name": "ROUNDED_RECTANGLE"
      },
      "text": "NS4-4 · ADD-ON MODULE — pick the one that matches the working diagnosis\nNeck module (ND1, ND2, ND5): NDI; range of movement; endurance hold; work-break log.\nWhiplash module (ND3, ND4): NDI, Quebec grade, stress-reaction screen (e.g. Impact of Event Scale), dizziness and concentration checklist.\nArm-pain module (ND7, ND8): arm pain 0–10 apart from neck pain; upper-limb tension test; strength and feeling by root at every visit (any new weakness → N6).\nHeadache module (ND9): headache diary (days per month, intensity, medicine days); flexion-rotation range; HIT-6 headache impact questionnaire.\nUpper-back module (ND6, ND10): thoracic rotation; chest expansion; pain on deep breath 0–10.\nYellow-flag module (ND4, ND12, or Örebro 50+): Örebro; Central Sensitization Inventory; PHQ-9 mood screen → doctor if moderate or worse; sleep.\nBone-health module (ND11): height to the millimetre; back-of-head-to-wall distance; Timed Up-and-Go; falls in the last year."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:8374",
      "type": "connector",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "1:8374",
        "x": "1100",
        "y": "1712",
        "connectorStart": "1:7263",
        "connectorStartCap": "NONE",
        "connectorEnd": "1:7271",
        "connectorEndCap": "ARROW_LINES"
      },
      "text": "NS4-2&gt;NS4-4"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:7275",
      "type": "shape-with-text",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "1:7275",
        "x": "1620",
        "y": "1816",
        "width": "460",
        "height": "349",
        "name": "ROUNDED_RECTANGLE"
      },
      "text": "PAIN RULES FOR HOME EXERCISE\n• Pain up to about 5 out of 10 during exercise is acceptable if it has settled back to its usual level by the next morning. If not, hold or step down one level.\n• Arm-symptom rule: symptoms moving up toward the neck = good; spreading down the arm, or new numbness or weakness = stop that exercise and re-check NT3 / N6.\n• Dizziness, double vision, or speech or swallowing trouble during exercise → stop at once and go to N3."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:7279",
      "type": "shape-with-text",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "1:7279",
        "x": "840",
        "y": "2530",
        "width": "520",
        "height": "197",
        "name": "ROUNDED_RECTANGLE"
      },
      "text": "NS4-5 · WEEK 1 — dose check\nASK: “Did the pain settle back to normal by the next morning after exercising? Have the arm symptoms or headaches changed?”"
    },
    {
